ter all.  Fail, and burn.',14,0,100,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Image of Archduke Calcinder'),(47309,0,0,'You will suffer!  You will face the wrath of the Twilight\'s Hammer!',12,0,100,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Minister Kiyuubi'),(47310,0,0,'Only pain awaits you!',12,0,100,1,0,0,0,0,0,'Minister Letherio'),(2755,0,0,'What?  $n, you served me well, but...',12,0,0,0,0,0,0,842,0,'Myzrael'),(2755,1,0,'Why have you summoned me so soon?  I haven\'t yet reached my full power!',12,0,0,0,0,0,0,843,0,'Myzrael'),(2755,2,0,'No matter.  You were a fool to help me, and now you will pay!',12,0,0,0,0,0,0,844,0,'Myzrael'),(3287,0,0,'Go swiftly, $n. My fate is in your hands.',12,1,100,1,0,0,0,1341,0,'Hana\'zua to Player'),(1402,0,3,'It\'s all their fault, stupid orcs. Had to burn my farm to the ground.',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,187,0,'Topper McNabb'),(1402,0,4,'Spare some change for a poor blind man? ...What do you mean I\'m not blind? ...I\'M NOT BLIND! I CAN SEE!! It\'s a miracle!',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,184,0,'Topper McNabb'),(1402,0,5,'Alms for the poor?',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,181,0,'Topper McNabb'),(1402,0,6,'I will gladly pay you Tuesday for a hamburger today.',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,182,0,'Topper McNabb'),(1402,0,7,'It\'s all their fault, stupid Alliance army. Just had to build their towers right behind my farm.',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,186,0,'Topper McNabb'),(5734,0,0,'Hmm, it would seem Keever needs a new subject. If that fool Abernathy keeps taking Keever\'s subjects, Keever may have to have a word with him.',12,33,100,1,0,0,0,2061,0,'Apothecary Keever <Royal Apothecary Society>'),(5734,1,0,'Ahh, there we go. Now, Keever must try this vial and see if it works.',12,33,100,1,0,0,0,2062,0,'Apothecary Keever <Royal Apothecary Society>'),(5734,2,0,'%s forces the fluid down the weary man\'s throat.',16,0,100,0,0,0,0,2075,0,'Apothecary Keever <Royal Apothecary Society>'),(5734,3,0,'%s pokes the small toad.',16,0,100,0,0,0,0,2064,0,'Apothecary Keever <Royal Apothecary Society>'),(5734,4,0,'Not what Keever was hoping for. Keever may have added too much earthroot. Let\'s see if the second serum will do what Keever needs.',12,33,100,1,0,0,0,2063,0,'Apothecary Keever <Royal Apothecary Society>'),(5734,5,0,'%s feeds the toad some of the strange liquid.',16,0,100,0,0,0,0,2065,0,'Apothecary Keever <Royal Apothecary Society>'),(5734,6,0,'%s pokes the small fuzzy squirrel with obvious disappointment.',16,0,100,0,0,0,0,2066,0,'Apothecary Keever <Royal Apothecary Society>'),(5734,7,0,'Well, that is just not right. The creature is far too small. Let us see what Keever\'s third batch will do.',12,33,100,1,0,0,0,2067,0,'Apothecary Keever <Royal Apothecary Society>'),(5734,8,0,'%s feeds the squirrel some of the viscous fluid.',16,0,100,0,0,0,0,2068,0,'Apothecary Keever <Royal Apothecary Society>'),(5734,9,0,'%s pokes the skittish rabbit.',16,0,100,0,0,0,0,2069,0,'Apothecary Keever <Royal Apothecary Society>'),(5734,10,0,'Keever is unhappy with this. Perhaps if Keever were to try a larger dose, that may fix this dilemma.',12,33,100,1,0,0,0,2070,0,'Apothecary Keever <Royal Apothecary Society>'),(5734,11,0,'%s grabs the rabbit and pours the fluid down its throat, then sets it back inside the cage.',16,0,100,0,0,0,0,2071,0,'Apothecary Keever <Royal Apothecary Society>'),(5734,12,0,'What is this? Did Keever ask for a sheep? Keever wanted a weapon of great power and all he got was this sheep. Keever is very disappointed.',12,33,100,1,0,0,0,2072,0,'Apothecary Keever <Royal Apothecary Society>'),(5734,13,0,'%s pokes the wooly sheep repeatedly.',16,0,100,0,0,0,0,2073,0,'Apothecary Keever <Royal Apothecary Society>'),(5734,14,0,'Keever is most pleased.',12,33,100,11,0,0,0,2074,0,'Apothecary Keever <Royal Apothecary Society>'),(36217,0,0,'I\'ve got my eye on you, Faranell.',12,1,100,1,0,0,0,36299,0,'Overseer Kraggosh'),(36217,1,0,'No abominations protecting you. No secrecy. No plotting in the dark.',12,1,100,0,0,0,0,36300,0,'Overseer Kraggosh'),(36217,2,0,'If you so much as spit without my permission, this place shuts down. Forcefully.',12,1,100,0,0,0,0,36301,0,'Overseer Kraggosh'),(2055,0,0,'I assure you, overseer, the Royal Apothecary Society dearly wishes to make up for the tragic misguidance which ended so many lives.',12,1,100,0,0,0,0,36302,0,'Master Apothecary Faranell '),(2055,1,0,'We will cause you no trouble. We seek only to continue our research in peace.',12,1,100,0,0,0,0,36303,0,'Master Apothecary Faranell '),(36217,3,0,'We\'ll see about that.',12,1,100,1,0,0,0,36304,0,'Overseer Kraggosh'),(36217,4,0,'Get that rotten nut to shut his trap!',12,1,100,5,0,0,0,36305,0,'Overseer Kraggosh'),(36213,0,0,'Shut your face, you gibbering idiot!',12,1,100,0,0,0,0,36306,0,'Undercity Guardian'),(5662,0,0,'You sorry sacks of maggot flesh can do better than that, now prove it!',12,33,100,25,0,0,0,1969,0,'Sergeant Houser'),(5662,0,1,'Alright you sorry sacks of bones. Let\'s see what you\'ve got. Strike your opponent, and don\'t stop till I say so.',12,33,100,1,0,0,0,1963,0,'Sergeant Houser'),(5662,0,2,'What do you call that? If that\'s fighting then I\'m Lothar himself!',12,33,100,25,0,0,0,1971,0,'Sergeant Houser'),(5662,0,3,'These piles of wood and straw may show mercy, but the Lich King won\'t!',12,33,100,25,0,0,0,1968,0,'Sergeant Houser'),(5662,0,4,'The sword isn\'t a tool, it\'s an extension of you. I expect better!',12,33,100,25,0,0,0,1970,0,'Sergeant Houser'),(5662,0,5,'Stop! You maggots call that fighting? That is pathetic! Now put your hearts in it, you don\'t need them anymore anyway!',12,33,100,25,0,0,0,1964,0,'Sergeant Houser'),(5662,0,6,'You\'re dead, not buried. Now show me your best!',12,33,100,25,0,0,0,1967,0,'Sergeant Houser'),(5662,0,7,'You don\'t fight for yourselves anymore, maggots! You fight for the Queen now so show me something worthy of her!',12,33,100,25,0,0,0,1966,0,'Sergeant Houser'),(5700,0,0,'If I could just find \"Magic and the Ways of Power\". Ahh here it is, what was it doing over here?',12,33,100,0,0,0,0,2034,0,'Samantha Shackleton'),(5700,0,1,'Very interesting. But if that\'s the case then my theory is wrong. I must reread the other sections to see what I missed.',12,33,100,1,0,0,0,2040,0,'Samantha Shackleton'),(5700,0,2,'Magical Flows and How They Effect the World\", by Maginor Dumas. That\'s the one I was looking for.',12,33,100,0,0,0,0,2030,0,'Samantha Shackleton'),(5700,0,3,'If this is correct then I have a lot more research to do.',12,33,100,1,0,0,0,2042,0,'Samantha Shackleton'),(5700,0,4,'Ahh there it is.',12,33,100,0,0,0,0,2029,0,'Samantha Shackleton'),(5700,0,5,'I really need a better system for filing these books. Ahh that\'s the one I wanted.',12,33,100,0,0,0,0,2031,0,'Samantha Shackleton'),(5700,0,6,'But this can\'t be right. Where did I put that other book?',12,33,100,1,0,0,0,2043,0,'Samantha Shackleton'),(5700,0,7,'\"Khadgar\'s Mystical Journal, Volume 8.\" I think this is the one I wanted.',12,33,100,0,0,0,0,2032,0,'Samantha Shackleton'),(5700,0,8,'Ahh, \"Mystical Conjurings of the Archmages of Dalaran.\" Perfect.',12,33,100,0,0,0,0,2033,0,'Samantha Shackleton'),(5700,0,9,'If I could just find \"Magic and the Ways of Power\". Ahh here it is, what was it doing over here?',12,33,100,0,0,0,0,2034,0,'Samantha Shackleton'),(5700,0,10,'\"Magic Maladies\", no. \"Magic Matricies\", no. Ahh here we go \"Magic Mysteries\".',12,33,100,0,0,0,0,2035,0,'Samantha Shackleton'),(5700,0,11,'There\'s the mystical tome I was looking for.',12,33,100,0,0,0,0,2036,0,'Samantha Shackleton'),(5700,0,12,'Yes, yes. Hmm, it seems to cross reference another tome. Guess I have to find that one too.',12,33,100,0,0,0,0,2037,0,'Samantha Shackleton'),(5700,0,13,'That wasn\'t very helpful. Let me check the other one.',12,33,100,0,0,0,0,2038,0,'Samantha Shackleton'),(5700,0,14,'That\'s what I wanted to know. Now I just need to find where the flux variance is discussed.',12,33,100,0,0,0,0,2039,0,'Samantha Shackleton'),(5700,0,15,'So I was right about the energies. Let\'s see what the other tome has to say on the subject.',12,33,100,0,0,0,0,2041,0,'Samantha Shackleton'),(5696,0,0,'Theresa, take this to Father Lankester.',12,33,100,1,0,0,0,1995,0,'Gerard Abernathy'),(5696,1,0,'Why thank you, my pet.',12,33,100,1,0,0,0,2011,0,'Gerard Abernathy'),(5696,2,0,'As good as I told you it would be, yes?',12,33,100,1,0,0,0,2003,0,'Gerard Abernathy'),(5696,2,1,'Didn\'t I tell you my new domination techniques would work?',12,33,100,1,0,0,0,2002,0,'Gerard Abernathy'),(5696,2,2,'So what do you think of my new toy?',12,33,100,1,0,0,0,1994,0,'Gerard Abernathy'),(5696,2,3,'How do you like my pet?',12,33,100,1,0,0,0,2000,0,'Gerard Abernathy'),(5696,3,0,'A little torture, a pinch of magic, and an ample helping of invasive surgery. She was conscious, of course.',12,33,100,1,0,0,0,2007,0,'Gerard Abernathy'),(5696,3,1,'Everyone has a weakness, it\'s just a matter of finding it.',12,33,100,1,0,0,0,2008,0,'Gerard Abernathy'),(5696,3,2,'It was simple once I broke her spirit.',12,33,100,1,0,0,0,2004,0,'Gerard Abernathy'),(5696,3,3,'I managed to discover that certain parts of the brain when removed or stimulated will make a subject much more docile.',12,33,100,1,0,0,0,2009,0,'Gerard Abernathy'),(5696,3,4,'You don\'t expect me to give up all my secrets do you?',12,33,100,1,0,0,0,2005,0,'Gerard Abernathy'),(5696,3,5,'A little ritual torture can go a long way.',12,33,100,1,0,0,0,2006,0,'Gerard Abernathy'),(5697,0,0,'Yes My Lord.',12,33,100,0,0,0,0,1998,0,'Theresa'),(5697,1,0,'My Lord Abernathy sends this to you.',12,33,100,0,0,0,0,1997,0,'Theresa'),(5697,2,0,'My Lord. From Father Lankester.',12,33,100,0,0,0,0,1999,0,'Theresa'),(5698,0,0,'Bravo, Gerard, you have exceeded yourself, yet again.',12,33,100,1,0,0,0,2018,0,'Joanna Whitehall'),(5698,0,1,'I am truly impressed, Gerard. I thought you were all talk, but I see I have been proven wrong.',12,33,100,1,0,0,0,2019,0,'Joanna Whitehall'),(5698,0,2,'I don\'t agree with your turning to alchemy to fix some of the problems, but I do agree with the results. Very well done.',12,33,100,0,0,0,0,2024,0,'Joanna Whitehall'),(5698,0,3,'Did you have to house train her, Gerard?',12,33,100,1,0,0,0,2027,0,'Joanna Whitehall'),(5698,0,4,'An amazing discovery you have made. I would love an opportunity to look at all of the failed experiments.',12,33,100,0,0,0,0,2023,0,'Joanna Whitehall'),(5699,0,0,'I\'ve never seen anything like it. No concentration or loss of awareness while the subject is dominated. What did you do to her?',12,33,100,1,0,0,0,2017,0,'Leona Tharpe'),(5699,0,1,'Amazing! How did you manage a permanent dominate?',12,33,100,1,0,0,0,2013,0,'Leona Tharpe'),(5699,0,2,'I don\'t approve of your experiments, Gerard, but I must admit the results are impressive. What exactly did you do to her?',12,33,100,1,0,0,0,2014,0,'Leona Tharpe'),(5699,0,3,'She retains knowledge and speech, and even the self sufficiency to perform tasks for you. Precisely what did you do?',12,33,100,1,0,0,0,2016,0,'Leona Tharpe'),(5699,0,4,'Truly amazing, Gerard. How did you do it?',12,33,100,1,0,0,0,2012,0,'Leona Tharpe'),(4607,0,0,'Ugh! What is that scoundrel doing sending his vermin to me? Get out of my sight before I take what is left of your life. And take this with you.',12,33,100,1,0,0,0,2028,0,'Father Lankester'),(5661,0,0,'Edward. Tyler. Prepare for your first challenge.',12,33,100,1,0,0,0,1978,0,'Brother Malach'),(5661,1,0,'Lysta, summon in the captives.',12,33,100,0,0,0,0,1977,0,'Brother Malach'),(5661,2,0,'Not a challenge at all it seems. Let us see how you handle your second test. Lysta, bring forth the minions of the Lich King.',12,33,100,0,0,0,0,1980,0,'Brother Malach'),(5661,3,0,'Lysta, summon in undead captives.',12,33,100,0,0,0,0,8306,0,'Brother Malach'),(5661,4,0,'It is time to face your final challenge young warriors! Prepare for your hardest fight yet.',12,33,100,0,0,0,0,1984,0,'Brother Malach'),(5661,5,0,'Lysta, summon forth... the abomination!',12,33,100,0,0,0,0,8307,0,'Brother Malach'),(5661,6,0,'Well done Edward and Tyler. You are progressing along in your training quite nicely. We shall test your mettle again soon.',12,33,100,0,0,0,0,1985,0,'Brother Malach'),(18303,0,0,'My brothers and sisters. Listen to me. We must speak of the survival of our people. We have narrowly survived one calamity, but I fear the next shall destroy us.',12,0,100,1,0,0,0,15673,0,'Lyria Skystrider'),(18303,1,0,'Can you not see what is happening? Open your eyes. It is laid bare for all to see. What is this new alliance? Why have we betrayed our allies of old, only to take up with the enemies of all that live?',12,0,100,1,0,0,0,15674,0,'Lyria Skystrider'),(18668,0,0,'No, you\'re wrong! We were the ones betrayed!',12,0,100,22,0,0,0,15675,0,'Vaeron Kormar'),(18669,0,0,'When have the dwarves ever been our friends?',12,0,100,11,0,0,0,15676,0,'Terric Brightwind'),(18724,0,0,'The humans abandoned us in our darkest hour! Their prince himself led the assault on our lands.',12,0,100,25,0,0,0,15677,0,'Melaya Tassier'),(18671,0,0,'You fool! The prince\'s minions were the very Forsaken we have now allied ourselves with, and now he has betrayed us!',12,0,100,5,0,0,0,15678,0,'Priest Ennas'),(18668,1,0,'The Ranger-General of Silvermoon will be a loyal ally!',12,0,100,1,0,0,0,15679,0,'Vaeron Kormar'),(18303,2,0,'You speak of her as friend? You are a fool. This \"Dark Lady\" is not Sylvanas.',12,0,100,1,0,0,0,15680,0,'Lyria Skystrider'),(18668,2,0,'Blood will be true. We can trust in none but our own!',12,0,100,25,0,0,0,15738,0,'Vaeron Kormar'),(18303,3,0,'Blood? And these orcs, these fair weather friends? They will aid us?',12,0,100,11,0,0,0,15743,0,'Lyria Skystrider'),(18671,1,0,'A great blight lies across our land! It grows every day. Our need for magic weakens us, and will bring us to destruction, just as it has before!',12,0,100,25,0,0,0,15744,0,'Priest Ennas'),(18669,1,0,'How are we to live without magic?',12,0,100,5,0,0,0,15745,0,'Terric Brightwind'),(18724,1,0,'Look at the wonders of this city! This is magic.',12,0,100,5,0,0,0,15747,0,'Melaya Tassier'),(18671,2,0,'But at what cost? You\'ve all been blinded. We have all been blinded.',12,0,100,1,0,0,0,15748,0,'Priest Ennas'),(18668,3,0,'You call us traitors?',12,0,100,25,0,0,0,15749,0,'Vaeron Kormar'),(18303,4,0,'The magisters are the traitors! They have sealed our doom.',12,0,100,25,0,0,0,15750,0,'Lyria Skystrider'),(18669,2,0,'Idealistic blather. Go back to your forests!',12,0,100,3,0,0,0,15751,0,'Terric Brightwind'),(18724,2,0,'You would have us live like the savages!',12,0,100,5,0,0,0,15752,0,'Melaya Tassier'),(18671,3,0,'No, not savagery! Conscience. The excesses of our people will destroy us, and all that we have struggled to build.',12,0,100,1,0,0,0,15753,0,'Priest Ennas'),(18303,5,0,'We have not struggled so hard to survive, only to bring about the true destruction.',12,0,100,1,0,0,0,15754,0,'Lyria Skystrider'),(18671,4,0,'We stand on the brink of destruction. We must reconsider this rash course of action.',12,0,100,5,0,0,0,15756,0,'Priest Ennas'),(18303,6,0,'If we speak as one, we cannot be ignored!',12,0,100,1,0,0,0,15917,0,'Lyria Skystrider'),(18671,5,0,'Lend us your voices! Now is the time we must act to save our people.',12,0,100,1,0,0,0,15918,0,'Priest Ennas'),(18671,6,0,'Lor\'themar must hear us! We will not be silenced!',12,0,100,5,0,0,0,15919,0,'Priest Ennas'),(18337,0,0,'That should take care of that. Summon me if you have further need of my services.',12,0,100,11,0,0,0,15922,0,'Priest Kath\'mar'),(18303,7,0,'We will repay the betrayal of the Alliance! We shall never forget, and never forgive!',12,1,100,21,0,0,0,15930,0,'Lyria Skystrider'),(18671,7,0,'Lor\'themar has remade Silvermoon into something we may truly be proud of.',12,1,100,21,0,0,0,15924,0,'Priest Ennas'),(18671,8,0,'The magisters are wise and will plot a prosperous course for our future.',12,1,100,21,0,0,0,15926,0,'Priest Ennas'),(5700,0,16,'Back to the drawing board.',12,33,100,1,0,0,0,2044,0,'Samantha Shackleton'),(5696,2,4,'Isn\'t she just the most amazing little creation?',12,33,100,1,0,0,0,2001,0,'Gerard Abernathy'),(5698,0,6,'Very nice, Gerard. Next you will be breeding them.',12,33,100,1,0,0,0,2022,0,'Joanna Whitehall'),(5698,0,7,'Your pet is wonderful, Gerard, but she needs a collar with a bell I think.',12,33,100,1,0,0,0,2026,0,'Joanna Whitehall'),(18896,0,0,'Function: Intelligence Agents, Torturers',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,17390,0,'Exodar Holographic Emitter'),(18896,1,0,'The cruel sayaadi temptresses exemplify the subtler side of the Legion\'s nihilistic Crusade.',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,17399,0,'Exodar Holographic Emitter'),(18896,2,0,'They revel in causing anguish and pain - and their murderous interrogations are the stuff of nightmares.',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,17811,0,'Exodar Holographic Emitter'),(18896,3,0,'Felguard',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,16006,0,'Exodar Holographic Emitter'),(18896,4,0,'Species: Mo\'arg',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,17377,0,'Exodar Holographic Emitter'),(18896,5,0,'Affiliation: Burning Legion',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,17368,0,'Exodar Holographic Emitter'),(18896,6,0,'Function: Standard Soldiers',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,17397,0,'Exodar Holographic Emitter'),(18896,7,0,'Conscripted from the mo\'arg race, these warriors serve as the Legion\'s rank and file soldiers.',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,17406,0,'Exodar Holographic Emitter'),(18896,8,0,'They are fearless and unwaveringly loyal to their master\'s godlike will.',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,18308,0,'Exodar Holographic Emitter'),(18896,9,0,'Doomguard',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,15997,0,'Exodar Holographic Emitter'),(18896,10,0,'Species: Ered\'ruin',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,17367,0,'Exodar Holographic Emitter'),(18896,11,0,'Function: Shock Troops, Enforcers',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,17369,0,'Exodar Holographic Emitter'),(18896,12,0,'Powerful and deliberate, these winged aberrations are renowned across the cosmos for their brutality.',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,17370,0,'Exodar Holographic Emitter'),(18896,13,0,'The Doomguard are utterly devoted to their Pit Lord masters and revel in the destruction of worlds.',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,18311,0,'Exodar Holographic Emitter'),(18896,14,0,'Wrathguard',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,15998,0,'Exodar Holographic Emitter'),(18896,15,0,'Species: Eredar',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,17371,0,'Exodar Holographic Emitter'),(18896,16,0,'Function: Honor Guard',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,17389,0,'Exodar Holographic Emitter'),(18896,17,0,'Cunning and precise, the Wrathguard often protect the Legion\'s eredar masters.',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,17398,0,'Exodar Holographic Emitter'),(18896,18,0,'Their skill in battle should never be underestimated.',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,17810,0,'Exodar Holographic Emitter'),(18896,19,0,'Succubus',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,15999,0,'Exodar Holographic Emitter'),(18896,20,0,'Species: Sayaad',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,17372,0,'Exodar Holographic Emitter'),(18896,21,0,'Shivarra',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,16000,0,'Exodar Holographic Emitter'),(18896,22,0,'Species: Shivarra',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,17373,0,'Exodar Holographic Emitter'),(18896,23,0,'Function: Priestesses, Military Chaplains',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,17391,0,'Exodar Holographic Emitter'),(18896,24,0,'Devout and exceedingly charismatic, these priestesses live only to evangelize the power of Sargeras\' dread vision.',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,17400,0,'Exodar Holographic Emitter'),(18896,25,0,'They are the driving heart of the Burning Crusade.',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,17812,0,'Exodar Holographic Emitter'),(18896,26,0,'Dreadlord',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,16001,0,'Exodar Holographic Emitter'),(18896,27,0,'Species: Nathrezim',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,17374,0,'Exodar Holographic Emitter'),(18896,28,0,'Function: Secret Police, Interrogator',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,17392,0,'Exodar Holographic Emitter'),(18896,29,0,'The Nathrezim are merciless villains who feed upon the energies of mortal creatures.',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,17401,0,'Exodar Holographic Emitter'),(18896,30,0,'They utilize terror and subterfuge - often turning brother against brother as whole worlds fall before their dark influence.',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,17813,0,'Exodar Holographic Emitter'),(18896,31,0,'Eredar',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,16002,0,'Exodar Holographic Emitter'),(18896,32,0,'Function: Overlords, Strategists',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,17393,0,'Exodar Holographic Emitter'),(18896,33,0,'The cunning, powerful eredar warlocks were once our noble kinsmen.',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,17402,0,'Exodar Holographic Emitter'),(18896,34,0,'Yet they fell to the lure of Sargeras\' evil - and now they have become our most stalwart enemies.',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,18303,0,'Exodar Holographic Emitter'),(18896,35,0,'Pit Lord',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,16003,0,'Exodar Holographic Emitter'),(18896,36,0,'Species: Annihilan',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,17376,0,'Exodar Holographic Emitter'),(18896,37,0,'Function: Generals, Ground Commanders',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,17394,0,'Exodar Holographic Emitter'),(18896,38,0,'These colossal destroyers serve as the Legion\'s military commanders.',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,17403,0,'Exodar Holographic Emitter'),(18896,39,0,'They are as cruel as they are powerful - and revel in the destruction of all that exists.',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,18305,0,'Exodar Holographic Emitter'),(18896,40,0,'Gan\'arg',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,16004,0,'Exodar Holographic Emitter'),(18896,41,0,'Function: Tinkerers, Machine-smiths',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,17395,0,'Exodar Holographic Emitter'),(18896,42,0,'These stunted mo\'arg are very clever, and are often employed as helpers for their larger brethren.',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,17404,0,'Exodar Holographic Emitter'),(18896,43,0,'Mischievous by nature, they are fond of employing their own hastily-constructed technologies.',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,17815,0,'Exodar Holographic Emitter'),(18896,44,0,'Mo\'arg',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,16005,0,'Exodar Holographic Emitter'),(18896,45,0,'Function: Engineers, Scientists',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,17396,0,'Exodar Holographic Emitter'),(18896,46,0,'Brutish though they seem, these iron-stitched horrors are exceedingly brilliant engineers and forge-smiths.',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,17405,0,'Exodar Holographic Emitter'),(18896,47,0,'Their black iron constructs have sown death across a thousand worlds.',12,7,100,0,0,0,0,17817,0,'Exodar Holographic Emitter'),(701,0,0,'%s becomes enraged!',16,0,100,0,0,0,0,7798,0,'Bloodscalp Mystic'),(36913,0,0,'Cry out in torment... Let your pain overcome your might...',15,0,14.2857,0,0,0,0,38355,0,'Eye of the Lichking'),(36913,0,1,'Release yourself from the chains of life...',15,0,14.2857,0,0,0,0,38352,0,'Eye of the Lichking'),(36913,0,2,'The Lich King is unstoppable...',15,0,14.2857,0,0,0,0,38350,0,'Eye of the Lichking'),(36913,0,3,'The Master\'s will remains inviolate...',15,0,14.2857,0,0,0,0,38347,0,'Eye of the Lichking'),(36913,0,4,'You cannot escape the Master\'s Wrath...',15,0,14.2857,0,0,0,0,38348,0,'Eye of the Lichking'),(36913,0,5,'Death consumes you...',15,0,14.2857,0,0,0,0,38353,0,'Eye of the Lichking'),(36913,0,6,'Give in... to the cold embrace of death...',15,0,14.2857,0,0,0,0,38351,0,'Eye of the Lichking'),(26531,0,0,'%s is entranced by the sun\'s reflection on Zeh\'gehn\'s knife.',16,0,100,0,0,0,0,25732,0,'Mesmerized Frog'),(26531,1,0,'%s croaks eagerly while directing its gaze to the docked ship.',16,0,100,0,0,0,0,25733,0,'Mesmerized Frog'),(24525,0,0,'Ku into me carver, ye ugly croaker!  Ku and show me who dares cross me brethren!',12,0,100,0,0,0,0,25734,0,'Zeh\'gehn'),(24525,1,0,'Dis a rankin\' set, mon, no scurvy dog gonna kass-kass me buckos an\' walk aweh! ',12,0,100,0,0,0,0,23581,0,'Zeh\'gehn'),(20239,0,0,'As the neutralizing agent mixes into the waters of the lake, the water that was irradiated by the crystal seems to clear.',16,0,100,0,0,0,0,17912,0,'Neutralizing Emote Placeholder'),(16514,0,0,'Tedon, go ahead and try the neutralizing agent on the mutated creature.',12,0,100,1,0,0,0,17938,0,'Botanist Taerix'),(20227,0,0,'Looks like it\'s time to let you out of this cage.',12,0,100,1,0,0,0,17925,0,'Apprentice Tedon'),(20227,1,0,'Now, to put the neutralizing agent on it...',12,0,100,0,0,0,0,17934,0,'Apprentice Tedon'),(20227,2,0,'Success!',12,0,100,71,0,0,0,17939,0,'Apprentice Tedon'),(24642,0,0,'Nothin\' finer than enjoying a fine beverage and the company of some fine buckos... hic!',12,0,100,1,0,0,0,23657,0,'Drunken Northse